<article class="env-lemma" id="00IF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00IF">Lemma <span data-tag="00IF">10.50.14</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a valuation ring. The valuation $v : A -\{ 0\}  \to \Gamma _{\geq 0}$ has the following properties: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$v(a) = 0 \Leftrightarrow a \in A^*$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$v(ab) = v(a) + v(b)$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$v(a + b) \geq \min (v(a), v(b))$ provided $a + b \not= 0$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>